//----------------------------------------------------------
// Weekly Cycle
// The length of the Castle Siege cycle.
//   Cycle (days): How many days one Castle Siege cycle lasts. The days of the next part must fit inside it.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~31]
//  CycleDays
//----------------------------------------------------------
    7            //Total amount of days event cycle last
end

1
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Cycle Schedule
// When each state of the cycle starts. The comment at the end of each row names the state.
//   State: 1 registration, 2 idle, 3 register the Mark of the Lord, 4 idle, 5 notify the attacking guilds, 6 read the state of the siege, 7 siege start, 8 siege end, 9 end of the cycle.
//   Day: The day of the cycle when this state starts (the first day is 0).
//   Hour: The hour of that day, 0 to 23.
//   Minute: The minute of that hour, 0 to 59.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~9]    [0~31]    [0~23]    [0~59]
//  State    Day       Hour      Minute
//----------------------------------------------------------
    1        0         0         0         //Registration for Castle Siege
    2        1         23        59        //Idle
    3        2         0         0         //Register Mark Of The Lord
    4        3         0         0         //Idle
    5        4         12        0         //Castle Attack Guild Notification
    6        4         19        0         //Reading the state of Castle Siege
    7        6         20        0         //Start of Castle Siege event
    8        6         22        0         //End of Castle Siege event
    9        7         0         0         //End of Castle Siege cycle
end

2
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Castle NPCs
// The gates, statues and guardians of the castle: their side, defense and regeneration level, life and where they stand. The comment at the end of each row names the NPC.
//   NPC: The castle NPC or monster: gate, statue, tower, shield or slingshot.
//   Number: A number that tells apart NPCs of the same kind (for example gate 1 to 6).
//   Saved in the database: Yes: its life and levels are saved in the database between sieges.
//   Side: 1 Defenders' side | 2 Attackers' side
//   Defense level: The defense upgrade level it starts with.
//   Recovery level: The recovery upgrade level it starts with.
//   Max life: Its maximum life.
//   From X: Column where it stands (left edge of the area).
//   From Y: Row where it stands (top edge of the area).
